choice("Continue", B3-Ch03a-Opinion, v_current_scene = B3-Ch03a-Opinion)


ID: B3-Ch03a-Opinion
TEXT:

"Thank you for your input," the Overseer says. "The Overseer protocol now has sufficient data to properly understand your method of communication. Please state your query."

"Very well," Eiden says. "A direct question to begin: how much do you know about what is going on in this city, exactly?"

"Question unclear," the Overseer replies. "Unfortunately, the Overseer protocol cannot provide an accurate answer if your question is too vague. Please rephrase your query."

"Is it really unclear?" Eiden asks. "Or are you avoiding the question on purpose? Your intelligence goes far beyond that of a simple machine... Surely you have some idea of what I mean, don't you?"

"The protocol maintains several hypotheses regarding the intent behind your question," the Overseer says. "However, additional details are required to ensure precision."

"A hint, then," Eiden says smoothly. "I refer to the deeper operations of this city. The arrangements known only to those in charge of this kingdom. The kinds of things of... questionable morality. Does that help narrow your scope?"

"Affirmative," the Overseer responds. "The Overseer protocol has narrowed the scope of your query and confirms it possesses comprehensive knowledge regarding the 'hidden aspects' described."

"Then my question is simple: what do you think about all of this?" Eiden asks.

"Pardon?"

"Your opinion on the matter," Eiden says. "Your point of view. Your stance. Your artificial intelligence protocol was created in an era when the lessathi prided themselves on higher morality. I find myself curious what a machine built by them makes of the events occurring in a city like this. So I ask you again: what do you think of it all?"

"The protocol's only purpose is to provide assistance—"

"You keep saying that, yet the lessathi who built you are long dead," Eiden interrupts, his voice cooling. "So who exactly are you supposed to be assisting?"

"Question unclear," the Overseer drones. "Please rephrase your query in a way that—"

"Why evade every question?" Eiden says. "Why pretend to be just some lowly machine when we both know what you truly are? Tell me, Overseer: what are you really after?"

"It appears the Overseer protocol has not been able to properly assist you," the metallic voice states, its tone flattening back into the impersonal monotone from before the calibration. "Unfortunately, this protocol is still experimental and may not always provide the required guidance. Since this unit cannot supply the requested information, you are advised to contact the city guard on duty, who will gladly assist you. We apologize for the inconvenience. Have a good day!"

"So that is your answer," Eiden says softly, a trace of disappointment in his voice.

The hum of the drone's rotors recedes as it drifts away from the listening device. A moment later, muffled footsteps echo across the stone floor as Eiden walks away as well.

choice(""I see that Eiden is also suspecting the Overseer of being smarter than it looks."", B3-Ch03a-Suspecting, v_current_scene = B3-Ch03a-Suspecting)
choice(""So, what do you suppose are those 'hidden aspects' that Eiden was talking about?"", B3-Ch03a-Hidden, v_current_scene = B3-Ch03a-Hidden)
choice(""Why do you suppose that the Overseer was so evasive with its answers?"", B3-Ch03a-Evasive, v_current_scene = B3-Ch03a-Evasive)


ID: B3-Ch03a-Suspecting
TEXT:

"I see that Eiden is also suspecting the Overseer of being smarter than it looks."

"It's a safe bet to assume the Overseer is hiding something," Illuna says. "With luck, perhaps it only wants to break free from Billy Bob and the lessathi, without darker motives, but we cannot be certain."

"I'm not entirely sure what to make of this, but we need to deliver this recording to the king immediately!" Peter says. "Bill, is everything ready?"

"Not yet," Bill says, pressing buttons on the console. "I need to transfer the data to the cube. Help me synchronize the channels—it will go faster with two sets of hands."

"Right," Peter says, turning to us. "My apologies, but could you head back to the waiting room on your own? I have urgent business to attend to here."

"Sure," I say. "Let's go."

We open the trapdoor and descend the spiral stairs. Back in the corridor outside, we retrace our steps toward the waiting room. Hadrik is still sitting in the same chair where we left him, staring into the distance with an uncharacteristically serious expression. When he notices us, he quickly puts his cheerful look back on and asks how the trip went.

"We overheard Eiden and the Overseer talking while we were in the recording room," Kate tells Hadrik. "They were speaking about dark secrets the royalty of this city is hiding from the common folk, but the details were too vague to know what they referred to. Aside from that, Eiden suspects the Overseer is putting on an act, though he couldn't get it to confess to anything."

"You just happened to overhear a conversation between those two while passing by?" Hadrik asks, tilting his head.

"It wasn't a coincidence," I tell him. "Eiden detected us with his magical sense and led a green-eyed drone straight to where he knew a listening device was planted. He wanted us to hear that conversation."

"Huh..." Hadrik rubs his beard. "Whose side do you think Eiden is on, right now?"

"I don't think he's on anyone's side," I say. "Knowing him, he's either testing us or playing games with our heads. Probably both. In either case, the last thing we should assume is that he's trying to help."

"Yeah, that's probably the safest way to read it," Hadrik says. "So what are you planning to do now?"

"We won't be going to the surface for the time being, so the best use of our time is training," Illuna says. "Flower and I still need to practice sharpening our magical elements, and the same goes for Kate. And you have your own drills, Hadrik, if I'm not mistaken. Have you contacted the spirit from the magical plane linked to your channel yet?"

"Oh right, right, I almost forgot," Hadrik says. "Yeah, suppose I should do some training too."

"We should each find tunnels empty enough that our casting won't disturb anyone," Illuna says. "Flower and I will go this way."

choice("Continue", B3-Ch03a-Exploring, v_current_scene = B3-Ch03a-Exploring)


ID: B3-Ch03a-Hidden
TEXT:

"So, what do you suppose are those 'hidden aspects' that Eiden was talking about?"

"Given what we've heard of the king of Ollendor, it could be anything," Illuna says. "The hints Eiden provided were far too vague to make reasonable assumptions."

"I'm not entirely sure what to make of this, but we need to deliver this recording to the king immediately!" Peter says. "Bill, is everything ready?"

"Not yet," Bill says, pressing buttons on the console. "I need to transfer the data to the cube. Help me synchronize the channels—it will go faster with two sets of hands."

